  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual assertion and visual scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'see? i fuckin told you!' and the visual scene of the two men interacting with the oven. The phrase 'see?' directly addresses the viewer, inviting them to witness and validate the claim being made. The visual scene of the men with the oven serves as the evidence for the textual assertion, creating a direct projection of the user as the one who is supposed to 'see' and understand the implied message. The user is also implicitly projected onto the scene as the one who is being told 'you were right' or 'you should have believed me' by the speaker (one of the men).",
